                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I realize you copy/pasted this but I think this should stop.  https://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/readability/avoid-const-params-in-decls.html"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 831,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "To keep things simple I would generally prefer to leave all refactoring for the separate change, so it would be easier to understand the change\n\nIf it is necessary we can correct it in a separate commit for all the similar cases"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 831,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah that's fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 836,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "would std::format be preferable to all this string concatenation?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 836,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "To keep things simple I would generally prefer to leave all refactoring for the separate change, so it would be easier to understand the change\n\nIf we want to refactor this function as well, I think it would be more clear if it would be done in a separate commit for all the similar cases"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 836,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Agree that we should stick to patterns.  I didn't realize this was also copy/pasted."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 853,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "What about something like:\n\nreturn std::format(\"Unknown {}\", rate_unit);"
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 853,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Konstantin Aladyshev",
                        "email": "aladyshev22@gmail.com",
                        "username": "Kostr"
                    },
                    "message": "I think that `Unknown 86` wouldn't go well with other things in the output.\n\nAt least it should be something like `Unknown(86)` to go with https://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/56303403b476c3721ab9f17b51e0f090f1b34ed2/pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp#L995 or https://github.com/openbmc/pldm/blob/56303403b476c3721ab9f17b51e0f090f1b34ed2/pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp#L1033\n\nBut I'm not sure that we need another text name, like `Unknown` since it can get lost between real values like `None(0)`, `Unspecified(1)`.\n\nAnyway, the code for the statesets that I've linked above doesn't print something like `Unknown`, so I would say if we really would want to change it, we need to do it in a separate commit for all the similar case at once."
                },
                {
                    "file": "pldmtool/pldm_platform_cmd.cpp",
                    "line": 853,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Fair point!"
                }
            ],
